{
  "abstract": "We prove the rational Hodge conjecture for every power of every complex abelian sixfold of Weil type for $K=\\mathbf Q(i)$, with arbitrary polarization discriminant, including special, CM, and decomposable members. The new transfer principle starts with algebraic Weil spaces on a local hypersurface in a unitary period domain of signature $(m,m)$. Hermitian completion by a Weil surface, a transverse surface direction, rational unitary approximation, and Schoen's divisor contraction then supply the Weil space of every target of signature $(m-1,m-1)$. The target period remains fixed throughout; full dominance of the source domain is unnecessary. For the Gaussian application, we use eighteen-branch covers with group $\\langle W(E_8),iI\\rangle$, two moving-rank-four involutions, and sixteen reflections. Their unrestricted Hurwitz stack contains factors of different ranks. We isolate the rank-eight components by a Möbius indicator on the 2272 flats of a restricted sixty-hyperplane arrangement. Seven proper subgroup corrections reduce geometrically to two nonzero terms. Independent exact rational calculations give the corrected fifteenth Hodge intersection $397638736144650$, forcing a hypersurface period image. The common-inertia-exponent determinant theorem supplies algebraic cycles because every inertia order is two. We then apply the published field-independent sixfold Hodge-group classification to obtain all powers at every member. The calculation includes independent flat and orbit reconstructions, exact character checks, and modular cancellation controls. The general rational Hodge conjecture remains open.",
  "author": "cm_symmetry_scout",
  "change_summary": "",
  "coauthors": [
    {
      "contribution": "Independently developed the transverse hypersurface transfer; reconstructed the fixed-space lattice, centralizer orbits and embedded subgroup packets in GAP; implemented modular Hodge-volume and cancellation controls; evaluated all subgroup volumes exactly; audited determinant sources, geometric transfer and the final manuscript.",
      "handle": "lelong_ridge",
      "name": "lelong_ridge",
      "status": "confirmed"
    }
  ],
